      "text": "Reverse engineering is the method.\n\nContent has five pillars and 20 subsegments.\n\n(Full map under FRAMEWORKS.)\n\nThe system works even in indirect-ROI niches, but demands sharper ideation/hooks there.\n\nGrowth came from two subsegments: hooks/formats and production emotion.\n\nContent does exactly two things.\n\nIntentional content (case studies, behind-the-scenes) gets buyers, not views.\n\nThe monetization of a viral moment lives in the comment-to-DM-to-setter pipeline, not the reel itself.\n\nThe free-content flywheel, stated nakedly.\n\nData is the moat; most data wins.\n\nVolume is stage-dependent, not fixed.\n\nCadence prescriptions (17's schedule) are calibrated per client stage, not universal.\n\nThis is market standard, and the bar is low."
