      "text": "Push marketing keeps you one step behind the customer.\n\nPush = reactive data-chasing with thin margins at volume; pull = the ecosystem sells before contact.\n\nThe self-learning AI analogy.\n\nA push funnel needs constant external optimization; a brand ecosystem improves itself as it compounds.\n\nDM-closing economics vs closer-team economics.\n\nThe trust economy, decade-scale.\n\nThe 80/20 inversion: marketing-heavy, sales-light.\n\nObjection-handling belongs in content, pre-call.\n\nBuyers buy the vision, not deliverables.\n\nEcosystem assets are self-selling and permanent; ads are binary and mortal.\n\nProfile ads exist only to feed the self-selling ecosystem; the ecosystem is the moat.\n\nThe gym analogy: compounding foundation vs cyclical restarting."
