      "text": "Content can work against you; volume negates luck in outreach, not content.\n\nNo unique mechanism, no content.\n\nThe mechanism precedes the content engine — identical to Pulsify's order of operations (unique mechanism before content).\n\nEvery piece of content must stimulate the mechanism.\n\nThe trust economy frame.\n\nHis macro thesis = Pulsify's trust recession, framed positively. The shift he names: offers/frameworks -> people/brands.\n\nIndirect beats direct because it's harder.\n\nDifficulty is the moat; anyone can name-drop their mechanism, few can pre-frame it invisibly.\n\nIndirect messaging pre-positions the offer before the pitch.\n\nContent has no universal framework; messaging must be found per person.\n\nIntention over batch-production.\n\nThe credential stack."
