      "tags": [
        "cadence",
        "posting",
        "schedule"
      ],
      "text": "The schedule's attributed results.\n\nReels are for nurturing, not converting; people use them for the wrong job.\n\nReels warm existing attention; conversion happens elsewhere.\n\nNever let volume outrun quality.\n\nVisual proof must match verbal claims.\n\nThe verbal-visual alignment rule (the masterclass's most-repeated idea) applied to static posts: the grid's job is congruence between shown life and claimed results.\n\nStories deliver the last 10% that turns a potential buyer into a buyer.\n\nYou can always ask, provided you give more than you ask.\n\nCTA permission is earned by value surplus; the give/ask ratio governs CTA volume.\n\nCTA density is a brand-positioning decision.\n\nFewer CTAs signal a premium brand; CTA frequency is strategy, not habit.\n\nCollab posts buy another audience instantly."
