      "source_id": "lesson-36",
      "title": "Thirty-six content lessons: The 36 lessons",
      "tags": [
        "content",
        "lessons",
        "hook",
        "reel"
      ],
      "text": "1. **Write for one person.**\n\n2. **Publish before you're ready.**\n\n3. **Content as byproduct.** Sources:\n\n4. **Boring is the only real mistake.**\n\n5. **Your best content already happened.**\n\n6. **Say the thing everyone's thinking but won't post.**\n\n7. **Document, don't create.**\n\n8. **Niche down until it scares you.**\n\n9. **If you're not sick of saying it, they haven't heard it yet.**\n\n10. **One idea per post.**\n\n11. **Intention decides result.**\n\n12. **A repeatable format beats a lucky hit.**\n\n13. **Reach without trust is just noise.** (Core Claim 3.)\n\n14. **Sell to buyers, not followers.**\n\n15. **Show, don't explain.**\n\n16. **Talk to customers more than cameras.**\n\n17. **They decide before they tell you.**\n\n18. **Change one belief per post.**\n\n19. **Repurpose everything.**\n\n20. **Don't check the numbers for an hour after posting.**\n\n21. **Don't quit on a bad week.**\n\n22. **Confidence is a format.**\n\n23. **Edit on a different day than you shoot.**\n\n24. **Faces outperform graphics.**\n\n25. **Confused people don't buy.**\n\n26. **Energy transfers through the screen.**\n\n27. **Lower the production, raise the clarity.**\n\n28. **Trends are rented attention.**\n\n29. **Re-watch your old stuff.**\n\n30. **Write ideas down the second they arrive.**\n\n31. **Done teaches more than perfect.**\n\n32. **One good conversation is a week of content.**\n\n33. **The machine can copy your output, never your intention.**\n\n34. **Do less.**\n\n35. **Post the one that scares you.**\n\n36. **Most things don't work.**"
